+## Prospective harmless-construction and evidence-retention amendment
+
+This amendment supersedes only conflicting WP70 harmless CONSTRUCTION raw-capture and physical owned-evidence limits in this prompt and its incorporated COMMON-E-CONTRACT. Historical runs, seals, raw failures, spent grants and UNKNOWN dispositions retain their original limits and meaning. It does not approve current source, runtime qualification, a retry, a TEST/P campaign or Original access. Normal independent source/checkpoint review and separate exact one-shot ROOT grants remain required before effects.
+
+Preserve ALL selected syscall events and statuses. The eight fixed offline construction commands may each retain at most 4,194,304 bytes shared across stdout, stderr and trace, with reservation before retention. Use the supported pathname-only -y option rather than -yy; no global status filter or parser broadening. Exact initial exec/argv/actor/epoch, control/framing/unknown-input and complete private EOF/exit checks remain mandatory. Functional outer cases retain their existing shared 2,097,152-byte stdout/stderr limit across compound calls. All 30s+2s cleanup, 120s preparation, 300s campaign, <=64 outer cases, 512MiB/10,000 construction-created entries, P/runtime/account/issuer/source/ownership/IO/wire/process/FD/RSS and earlier-clock limits remain unchanged. Evidence disk capacity is not runtime memory or spendable account credit.
+
+The complete physical owned E evidence, including every retained old failure and every subsequently published packet, must stay within 2,147,483,648 bytes and 4,096 regular files. The exact planning ledger below is normative for prospective class maxima and counts. Its 1,689,258,640-byte/2,987-file sum includes the frozen historical baseline, not a fresh actual remaining-cap receipt. No successful-completion prediction follows from a bounded retention plan.
+
+Before effects, implement and independently review source-owned pre-retention byte/file/class/combined-total reservations for EVERY writer, including temporary/replacement coexistence, raw streams, command/whole pairs, origins/transients, deployment inventories, outer/guardian/control/error records, aggregate results, catalogs/seals and review/publication overhead. Enforce encoded bounds BEFORE append/write and retained-buffer growth, with finite record cardinality, nested strings/argv/errors, escaping expansion and serializer memory. The 215 metadata pairs allocate at most 64KiB to command and 64KiB to whole. Other combined classes need explicit disjoint suballocations. A post-write scan or unbounded json.dumps followed by a quota check is insufficient.
+
+Reserve failure/cleanup/refusal/final-seal capacity before child launch or large metadata work, with a surviving owner able to report and reap within unchanged deadlines even if the coordinator allocation is exhausted. Overflow must refuse truthfully and preserve the complete retained bounded raw prefix with suffix/metadata UNKNOWN where necessary; a truncated or omitted successful record cannot qualify a tool. Controls must cover exact-limit/limit+one, bytes/files/cardinality, all writers and preflight/Popen/parse/serialization/raw-overflow/deadline/nonzero/abort/death/guardian cleanup paths. The source-specific finite construction and memory proof must be updated without raising its limits.
+
+Prospective exact immutable references may avoid duplicating already-admitted input/source metadata only when they bind literal path, bytes, SHA256, rights, closed member membership and original nested-seal meaning, with finite acyclic closure. Author and DIFFERENT reviewer must fully resolve and verify them; missing, changed, ambiguous or mutable targets refuse BEFORE effects. References grant no new source authority. Newly generated raw/errors/failures remain literal; no old raw or metadata may be moved, hidden, deleted, trimmed or retrospectively recapped, and no archive ratification is granted.
+
+The 16MiB/256-file DIFFERENT-review reserve is aggregate for all prospective reviews, including their failures and seals. Every later step must verify actual remaining byte/file/class capacity and reserve its complete failure envelope plus still-required disposition/review. The 128MiB failure reserve and unallocated headroom are capacity planning, never permission for another attempt or silent borrowing from another class. A new unclassified writer or insufficient allocation stops for reviewed planning. The 275 prefix candidates and the entire unknown suffix remain unadmitted until separately bounded investigation and independent source/manifest review. All prior approval/source-custody requirements and full M1 obligations remain open; M2/PDF remain gated.
